    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'publication' can refer to both the act of publishing (e.g., 'the publication of the book') and a published item (e.g., 'a scientific publication'). The Japanese expression '公開' (kōkai) primarily means 'opening to the public,' 'making available to the public,' or 'public release/disclosure.' It does not cover the sense of 'a published item' and is too specific for the general 'act of publishing' (e.g., a book or magazine). Therefore, '公開' is semantically narrower than the English lemma and not a natural general equivalent for learners.",
    "suggested_ja_replacement": {
      "surface": "出版",
      "reading": "しゅっぱん",
      "reason": "'出版' (shuppan) is a more general and appropriate term for 'publication' when referring to the act of publishing books, magazines, or other materials. While it doesn't explicitly cover the 'published item' sense (for which '出版物' would be used), it is a much better fit for the core concept of 'publication' as an act than '公開'."
    }
